The bounded comparison found the precise mismatch: the real continuation is the one-element `Stmts` list `Return(...) .Stmts`, while the invariant had matched the bare `Stmt`. I’m narrowing the invariant to that exact continuation and will re-prove it before reusing it.
apply patch
patch: completed
/workspace/spec.k
diff --git a/concrete_tests.py b/concrete_tests.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..5224af12e28d66cd769da110a39d6d1d12a522bb
--- /dev/null
+++ b/concrete_tests.py
@@ -0,0 +1,14 @@
+def hex_key(num):
+    count = 0
+    digit = ""
+    for digit in num:
+        count += digit in "2357BD"
+    return count
+
+
+assert hex_key("") == 0
+assert hex_key("AB") == 1
+assert hex_key("1077E") == 2
+assert hex_key("ABED1A33") == 4
+assert hex_key("123456789ABCDEF0") == 6
+assert hex_key("2020") == 2
